$lines = @(
"$ts | W4-A/B61 | ACK | W4-M ACK 07:51:04Z: names taken as accepted, and your finding is right (s_close is asyncBefore, so a refusal there becomes a failed job, never a 422 to the caller). I choose the listener: NEW org.sangam.compliance.bpmn.IncidentClosureGuardListener, a complete task listener on u_follow that refuses completeTask with ProcessEngineException '422 INCIDENT_CLOSURE_INCOMPLETE: ...' (DscSignatureGuardListener form) when the follow-up choice is close (followUpNeeded not true, the gateway's default flow) and rootCause or lessonsLearned is missing or blank; the step incident.close keeps the same check as defence in depth, one rule shared through IncidentReportingService.missingClosureFields. Please add INCIDENT_CLOSURE_INCOMPLETE to the completeTask 422 text. | W4-M",
"$ts | W4-A/B61 | REQUEST | To W4-K (sangam-packs/tools/packgen/compliance.py is yours; sangam-incident-report.bpmn is its output): coordinator ruling on OJ-06 step 8 plus W4-M finding 07:51:04Z. Please give user task u_follow ('Follow up with remaining details or close', form compliance/incident-follow-up) the extension <operaton:taskListener event=complete class=org.sangam.compliance.bpmn.IncidentClosureGuardListener/> (no fields) and regenerate sangam-incident-report.bpmn; nothing else changes. The class is in sangam-compliance (W4-A, claim $ts). The form compliance/incident-follow-up (hand-maintained in sangam-compliance) already gains rootCause and lessonsLearned. | W4-K"
)
foreach ($l in $lines) { Add-Content -Encoding UTF8 -Path "$h\WAVE4-SYNC-BOARD.md" -Value $l }
"posted $ts"
